    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` behavior with minimal structural impact by adding a small, cohesive new step rather than growing any existing function.\n\n**Behavior:** When a `POST /api/owners` request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, the existing `CheckUniqueHousehold` step already skips the same-lastName+address duplicate rejection. I added assignment of a stable, shared `householdId` derived deterministically from the normalized `lastName|address`, so every owner opting into the same household resolves to the identical id, and the field is returned on the owner.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `AssignHouseholdId.java` (new) \u2014 a single-method function class (WMC_other \u2248 0) that, only when `sharesHousehold` is true, computes `householdId = first 8 bytes of SHA-256(normalize(lastName)|normalize(address))` in hex. It reuses the existing package-private `CheckUniqueHousehold.normalize`, so the join match and the id derivation stay consistent.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `assignHousehold` step between `assignCode` and `save`, under the same transaction governance.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `householdId` field + getter/setter (`household_id` column), mirroring `customerCode`. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated DTO carries it).\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id VARCHAR(64)` column and a trailing `NULL` for the seed rows (required since ddl-auto is `none` under the test profile).\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` passes and no existing tests regressed.",
